From 07805a9448d43700fe8ac81fc01183856f36d554 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: stephan-xyz <stephan@zehrer.xyz>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 16:13:56 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 46/47] bcm2835-btuartd: the mini UART to the Pi 3B+ Bluetooth
 chip as a scheme

The serial console keeps the PL011, so the Bluetooth chip on GPIO 30 to
33 gets the mini UART (ALT5), as with Linux's miniuart-bt overlay:
/scheme/btuart/data is the byte stream, baud and clock set the baud rate
from the core clock. A thread moves received bytes into a buffer; RTS and
CTS flow control are on.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
